Guard ProfileDAO.getByUserURI against a null user URI.

/rest/vuejs/user_config is not @ApiProtected. A request without a valid
token resolves to AccountModel.getAnonymous(), whose URI is null. For a
non-admin, the front menu build calls
AccountDAO.getCredentialList(user.getUri()) -> ProfileDAO.getByUserURI(null).
SPARQLDeserializers.nodeURI(null) returns null, and the Jena query builder
renders the null triple object as the bare token "ANY", so GraphDB rejects
the query:
  MALFORMED QUERY: Lexical error ... Encountered: '125' ... after prefix "ANY"
The exception is swallowed by UserConfigService, so the menu silently
comes back empty and the SPA half-loads.

A principal with no URI is in no group user-profile, so return an empty
list instead of building a query.

Present in 1.5.4 and unfixed on upstream develop as of 2026-09-01.
Reported upstream: TODO(link).

